From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: pci_old: fix %#llx on 32-bit dma_addr_t

The tx-data diagnostic in rtw_pci_old_tx_isr() prints dma_addr_t values
with %#llx. dma_addr_t is a plain u32 on 32-bit targets (e.g. OpenWrt
23.05 mt76x8), so -Werror=format rejects that build. Cast both arguments
to unsigned long long, as the rest of the driver does when printing
64-bit DMA values.

Downstream build fix (null SHA): pci_old.c exists only in the
lwfinger/pkshih rtw88 trees at the pin and this diagnostic block prints
dma_addr_t directly; the fix applies to it without dependencies.
Note: repo-only compile fix, kept out of upstream flows; applies to the
pinned tree ahead of (and independently of) every other patch.
---
diff --git a/pci_old.c b/pci_old.c
index bb83b34..b3e2cef 100644
--- a/pci_old.c
+++ b/pci_old.c
@@ -352,7 +352,8 @@ static void rtw_pci_old_tx_isr(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev,
 		if (dma != tx_data->dma)
 			rtw_err(rtwdev,
 				"dma from tx_data %#llx != dma from tx_desc %#llx\n",
-				tx_data->dma, dma);
+				(unsigned long long)tx_data->dma,
+				(unsigned long long)dma);
 
 		dma_unmap_single(&rtwpci->pdev->dev, dma, skb->len,
 				 DMA_TO_DEVICE);
